  "query_preview": "(This evening through Saturday)...\nIssued at 216 PM EDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nQuiet weather will continue across central Indiana through the first \nhalf of next weekend. For much of the period, the area will be under \nnorthwest flow aloft with high pressure in control of the surface.\n\nA couple of cold fronts will move through during the next week. The \nfirst will be on Sunday. Forcing from the associated short wave will \nbe well north of the area, and there will be no moisture for the \nfront to work with as the Gulf will be cut off. Another front will \nmove through mid to late week next week, and it too will have no \nmoisture.\n\nHigh temperatures will remain near to above normal for most of the \nnext week. The exception will be Monday, which will be cooler with \nthe passage of the first cold front. While that second front will \nmove through later in the week, most guidance keeps cooler air out \nof the area.\n\nWith the cooler air Monday night, some locations will dip into the \nupper 30s. Cannot rule out some patchy frost in favored cold spots, \nespecially northeast.\n\nThe only other concern this week will be afternoon humidity values \naround 30 percent for some areas. With a drying ground, this could \ncause some increase in fire weather concerns. Will have to watch for \nthe potential for even lower humidity, as blended guidance can miss \nlower dewpoints from better mixing. Winds at least do not look to \nadd to any concern.",
